  "AICL is the licensing and transaction layer built on top of AICR. Where AICR declares what is allowed, AICL defines how permission is actually obtained: license tiers and prices, quote and payment endpoints, signed license tokens, usage and audit logs, and revocation. It is designed to interoperate with emerging machine-payment mechanisms such as HTTP 402 flows and pay-per-crawl schemes, with agentic payment kept inside human-approved budgets and audit trails.": "AICL ej layer in laisin im transaction eo kar kalōk ioon AICR. Ijo AICR ej kwaḷọk ta eo ekar kōtḷọk, AICL ej kōmmeḷeḷeik wāween bōk maroñ eo ilo ṃool: tier ko an laisin im oṇāān, endpoint ko ñan quote im kōḷḷā, token ko an laisin ewor sain, log ko an kōjerbal im audit, im revocation. Kar design e bwe en jerbal ippān mechanism ko ekāāl an machine-payment āinwōt HTTP 402 flow ko im pay-per-crawl scheme ko, im payment an agent ro ej pād wōt ilo budget eo armej ear kaṃool im audit trail ko.",
