  "AICR declares what AI systems may do with content — reading, summarization, transformation, RAG, training, commercial use, redistribution, attribution. AICL converts those rights into executable flows: authorization, payment, credentials, usage logs, and revocation. Rather than forcing a binary between total prohibition and free extraction, AICR/AICL enables tiered licensing markets, interoperating with emerging machine-payment mechanisms (HTTP 402, pay-per-crawl) while keeping agentic payment inside human-approved budgets and audit trails.": "AICR ej kwaḷọk ta eo AI systems remaroñ kōṃṃan kōn kontent — riit, summary, transformation, RAG, training, commercial use, redistribution, attribution. AICL ej ukot maroñ kein ñan flow ko emaroñ jerbal: authorization, kōḷḷā, credential ko, log in kōjerbal, im revocation. Jab kōṃṃan binary in aolep mọ ak extraction e jāmin kōḷḷā, AICR/AICL ej kōtḷọk market ko in laisin tiered, im jerbal ippān mechanism ko ekāāl an machine-payment (HTTP 402, pay-per-crawl), im payment an agent ro ej pād wōt ilo budget eo armej ear kaṃool im audit trail ko.",
  "AICR generator": "AICR generator",
