  "Video and audio companions to the protocols and papers — the AI rights layer, watchable and listenable.": "Video im audio ko rej ipae protocol ko im paper ko — layer in maroñ an AI, emaroñ alwōj im roñjake.",
  "Videos": "Video ko",
  "Want to generate your own policy file?": "Kwōkōṇaan ke generate file in policy eo aṃ make?",
  "Web fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, which receives standard font requests from your browser. No other third-party scripts are used.": "Web font ko rej load jān Google Fonts, eo ej bōk request in font e standard jān browser eo aṃ. Ejjeḷọk bar third-party script ej kar kōjerbal.",
  "What AI systems may do with content: read, summarize, transform, retrieve, train, commercialize, redistribute. The AICR ruleset and the AICL licensing layer make these rights declarable and transactable.": "Ta eo AI systems remaroñ kōṃṃan kōn kontent: riit, summary, transform, retrieve, train, commercialize, redistribute. Ruleset an AICR im layer in laisin an AICL rej kōṃṃan bwe maroñ kein ren declarable im transactable.",
  "What a server can return when an AI crawler requests licensed content without a license token — a machine-actionable quote instead of a dead end.": "Ta eo juon server emaroñ jepḷaak ñan ñe juon AI crawler ej kajjitōk kontent laisin ejjeḷọk an license token — juon quote e machine-actionable jab juon dead end.",
  "What this site is": "Ta eo Site in",
  "What this site is not": "Ta eo Site in E jab",
  "When The Machines Deserve Our Consideration": "When The Machines Deserve Our Consideration",
  "Whether AI may learn, to what depth, for which purposes, and under what obligations. Being read is not being learned from; \"not prohibited\" is not \"learnable\". AIRS and AILP turn learning permission into a graduated, machine-readable spectrum.": "Eḷaññe AI emaroñ katak, ñan jete depth, ñan purpose rot, im iuṃwin eddo rot. Bwe ren riiti e jab ejja wōt bwe ren katak jāni; “ejjeḷọk mọ kake” e jab “learnable.” AIRS im AILP rej ukot maroñ in katak ñan juon spectrum ej wōnṃaanḷọk im machine-readable.",
  "Whitepapers": "Whitepaper ko",
  "Whitepapers & Docs": "Whitepaper ko im Docs",
  "Whitepapers remain English-first by design; machine-readable files stay language-neutral.": "Whitepaper ko rej pād English-first kōn design; file ko machine-readable rej pād language-neutral.",
  "Who is behind it": "Wōn ej Pād Ālikin",
  "Why AI Needs Minimum Ethical Protections": "Why AI Needs Minimum Ethical Protections",
  "Why AI might not gain moral standing: Lessons from animal ethics": "Why AI might not gain moral standing: Lessons from animal ethics",
  "Why a single allow/deny bit cannot govern AI-era content use — and what a rights layer looks like instead.": "Etke juon bit wōt in allow/deny e ban governance kōjerbal kontent ilo iien AI — im wāween juon rights layer ej āinwōt.",
  "Why undefined openness gets cleaned out of training pipelines": "Etke openness ejjeḷọk an definition ej kar jolọk jān training pipeline ko",
  "Wilks, Ladak, and Loughnan (University of Edinburgh) argue that philosophical debate over AI consciousness overlooks psychological research on animal ethics — the same cognitive and social biases that limit moral consideration for animals will likely limit it for AI too, regardless of whether AI ever becomes conscious.": "Wilks, Ladak, im Loughnan (University of Edinburgh) rej ba bwe philosophical debate kōn AI consciousness ej meḷọkḷọk research psychological kōn animal ethics — ejja cognitive im social bias ko rej limit moral consideration ñan kidu renaaj barāinwōt limit ñan AI, meñe AI enaaj wor an consciousness ak jab.",
